    <string name="portal_alert_channel">Local parent alerts</string>
    <string name="portal_alert_explanation">Local periodic alerts are a fallback, not a guarantee. Android checks for new events at best every 15 minutes, often later to save battery. The institution server must be reachable, usually on the same Wi-Fi. When your institution configures the secure relay, remote alerts can also arrive through Firebase; they stay generic and never include a child’s name. No alert is guaranteed while offline.</string>
