    <string name="portal_institution">Connect to your institution</string>
    <string name="portal_intro_network">A network connection is required. Usually, connect to the same Wi-Fi as the institution computer. We search the local network; you can also enter an institution-provided HTTPS address. There is no central school directory: a code selects a child at the institution you choose, not a school anywhere on the internet. Confirm the address with your institution before signing in.</string>
    <string name="portal_intro_privacy">Each child has a separate institution and encrypted session. Adding children does not establish family relationships. Optional local alerts check the institution periodically on an accessible network. If your institution configures the secure relay, attendance updates can also arrive as remote notifications through Firebase; delivery is never guaranteed. Passwords, activation keys and child codes are never saved.</string>
    <string name="portal_intro_roles">Administrators manage access and parent codes. Employees use daily attendance tools. Parents see only children added with their own codes.</string>
